acceptance_criteria: "An episode specification is a declared, storable, shareable artifact naming the workspace recipe, the task item set, the observable and withheld field sets, the observation token budget, the grading criteria, and the run limits; A different machine and a different pm build within the supported format window can re-execute the same specification and obtain the same result; The public SDK opens an episode, exposes the bounded observation, scores it, and closes it with a recorded result, with no shelling out required; The agent acts through the ordinary pm surface only, with no episode-specific mutation API; Scoring reads recorded workspace state exclusively, and a negative control proves an episode fails to score when a grader consults state the history does not contain; Withheld grading fields are unreachable through every read surface available to the agent, proven by a test that attempts to read them from inside an episode; One benchmark, one evaluation, one training and one scale-transfer configuration all run on the same loop with no special path; A single item and a single episode work with no special path, and concurrent episodes share no mutable state; A worked exemplar in the repository runs a passing episode, a failing episode, and an episode that fails for the wrong reason"
parent: pm-8jdc
risk: high
confidence: 80
